      "schema:name": "antibody_reagent_kit",
      "schema:description": "The antibody reagent used to recognize a specific protein target or histone modification during the Paired-Tag assay. These antibodies bind to their target epitopes and direct the tagmentation reaction to the corresponding chromatin regions, enabling profiling of chromatin features in individual cells. If a custom antibody reagent is used, then enter \"Custom\". Example: Abcam; Anti-Histone H3 (tri methyl K9) antibody [EPR16601] - ChIP Grade; PN: ab176916",
      "pav:createdOn": "2026-07-27T11:17:32-07:00",
